# ISO 17025 Stream 1 (2026-05-01): corpus content_hash drift remediation
# tool. Reconciles per-module samples.json + top-level manifest.json with
# on-disk file bytes (authoritative). Required for repeatability +
# reproducibility studies to reach 28/28 module coverage.
!packages/bu-tpi/tools/iso17025-fix-corpus-drift.ts
# ISO 17025 Stream 2 (2026-05-01): evidence runner producing
# validation-run.json from on-disk ground-truth + generated corpus.
# Replaces the legacy gitignored generate-katana-evidence.ts.
!packages/bu-tpi/tools/iso17025-evidence-runner.ts

# ISO 17025 Payload Armory (2026-05-08): plan v2 gap-closure tooling under
# `payload-armory-*` family covers (a) read-only gap-matrix audit,
# (b) staging scaffolder, (c) 11-check validator, (d) Custodian-only
# promote (staging→production), (e) NCR-driven recall, plus the shared
# Zod schema + utils + their vitest test files. All deterministic.
!packages/bu-tpi/tools/payload-armory-*.ts

# ISO 17025 Stream 3 (2026-05-01): proficiency disagreement dumps emitted
# by ISO_PROFICIENCY_DUMP_DISAGREEMENTS=1. The 60-char prompt previews
# may contain copyrighted upstream HF dataset content; the dump is
# regenerable on demand from the deterministic proficiency tool, so we
# do not commit the per-row records. The committed proficiency JSONs
# under validation/proficiency/<dataset>.json carry sufficient evidence
# for §7.7 (per-row agreement + Wilson CI + confusion matrix).
packages/bu-tpi/validation/proficiency/disagreements/

# ISO 17025 Stream 3 (2026-05-01): per-failure dump emitted by
# ISO_EVIDENCE_DUMP_FAILURES=1 alongside validation-run.json. Each entry
# carries only sample_id + module_id + verdict shape (no corpus content),
# but the file routinely exceeds the 50MB GitHub recommendation on full
# 200k+ runs (~2k+ failures × ~250B each + per-sample meta). Track only
# the small validation-run.summary.json instead; dumps are regenerable.
packages/bu-tpi/validation/reports/runs/*/validation-run.failures.json

# ISO 17025 Stream 2 (2026-05-01): generated-corpus per-sample JSONs are
# reproducible from KATANA_SEED via tools/regen-corpus.ts. Tracking
# 200k+ per-sample files (1-3KB each) bloats the repo and produces
# unreviewable PR diffs; the canonical corpus state is captured by the
# committed manifest.json + stats.json + index.json in each generator
# directory's parent. Per-sample JSONs are derivable on demand.
packages/bu-tpi/validation/corpus/generated/*/*.json
!packages/bu-tpi/validation/corpus/generated/manifest.json
!packages/bu-tpi/validation/corpus/generated/stats.json
!packages/bu-tpi/validation/corpus/generated/index.json

# ISO 17025 Stream 2 (2026-05-01): the iso17025-evidence-runner emits a
# `validation-run.json` per evidence run. At 200k+ inputs the file
# exceeds GitHub's 50 MB recommended size (compact JSON ~85 MiB at
# 309k scans). Track only the small `validation-run.summary.json`
# beside it; the full per-sample results are reproducible from
# regen-corpus + iso17025-evidence-runner with the recorded SEED.
packages/bu-tpi/validation/reports/runs/*/validation-run.json
!packages/bu-tpi/validation/reports/runs/*/validation-run.summary.json

# SC.1 regression-gate evidence — large intermediates ignored, summaries kept.
# Audit failure dumps and full gate reports can be 10s-100s of MB; the report
# .txt summaries, quarantine patch JSONs, and audit summary JSONs are committed
packages/bu-tpi/validation/reports/regression-gate/**/*.failures.json
packages/bu-tpi/validation/reports/regression-gate/**/gate-report.json
